Then setting $n = \infty$ in the recursion $a_n = 1 + (a_n - 1)^2$ gives
\[p = 1 + (p-1)^2,\]so $(p-1)^2 + (p-1) - 1 = 0.$ (Since $p$ is clearly positive.)  By the quadratic formula,
\[p - 1 = \frac{-1 \pm \sqrt{1 + 4}}{2} = -1/2 \pm \sqrt{5}/2,\]so $p = -3/2 \pm \sqrt{5}/2.$  We must take the positive root.

Also,
\[a_0 a_1 \cdots a_n = 1 + (a_0 - 1)^2 \left( 1 + (a_1 - 1)^2 \right) \cdots \left( 1 + (a_{n - 1} - 1)^2 \right) \le 1 + \frac{1}{2} = \frac{3}{2},\]so it converges.

Note that $a_n - a_{n - 1} = (a_n - 1) - (a_{n - 1} - 1) = (a_{n - 1} - 1)^2 - (a_{n - 1} - 1) = (a_{n - 1} - 1)(a_{n - 1} - 2),$ so $a_{n + 1} - a_n = (a_{n} - 1)(a_{n} - 2)(a_{n - 1} - 1)(a_{n - 1} - 2) \ge 0 \implies a_{n + 1} \ge a_n$.  Let $x_n = a_n - 1,$ where $x_n > 0$.  Then
\[x_{n + 1} = (x_n + 1)(x_n)(x_{n - 1} + 1)(x_{n - 1}) = x_nx_{n - 1}(x_n + x_{n - 1} + 2),\]so $x_{n + 1} \ge 2x_n x_{n - 1}$, i.e.
\[\frac{x_n x_{n - 1}}{x_{n + 1}} \le \frac{1}{2}.\]Since $x_n$ is decreasing and bounded by 0, the given expression converges.  Furthermore,
\[x_0 x_1 \cdots \left( x_n \frac{x_{n - 1}}{x_{n + 1}} \right) \le x_1^n,\]so
\[\frac{x_1}{x_1 - 1} x_0 x_1 \cdots \left( x_n \frac{x_{n - 1}}{x_{n + 1}} \right) \le \frac{x_1}{x_:$ - 1}$, i.e.
\[x_0 x_1 \cdot \dotsm \cdot x_n \frac{x_{n-1}}{x_{n+1}} \cdot \frac{1}{x_1 - 1} \le \frac{x_1}{x_1 - 1} = 1.\]Hence, \[a_0 a_1 \cdots a_n\frac{a_{n - 1}}{a_{n + 1}} \frac{a_0}{a_1 - 1} \le 1.\][asy]
